  <h2>Frequently asked questions about builders and developers in Lucknow</h2>

  <h3>How many builders and developers operate in Lucknow?</h3>

  <p>Lucknow has several hundred registered construction firms of varying size and specialisation. The market includes large developers working on township projects, mid-size builders handling individual homes and small commercial blocks, and specialist contractors focused on civil work only. For residential plot owners, the mid-size builder segment is the most relevant. VP Infra operates in this segment with ISO certification and a documented quality process.</p>

  <h3>What documents should I check before hiring a builder in Lucknow?</h3>

  <p>Ask for GSTIN, MSME Udyam registration, ISO certificate if applicable, and at least one copy of a previous project's structural drawings and material test reports. Also ask for references you can call independently, not just names the builder provides who will only say good things. VP Infra's registration details are publicly verifiable: UDYAM-UP-50-0085926.</p>

  <h3>What is the difference between a contractor and a developer?</h3>

  <p>A contractor builds to a brief, on land you own, for a fee. A developer buys or aggregates land, plans a project, and sells units. Contractors are accountable for construction quality. Developers are accountable for delivery timelines, approvals, and common area maintenance. For custom home construction, you need a contractor or a builder, not a developer.</p>

